      "ReviewText": "I bought the insurance plan figuring this thing would not last. I have three other weed whackers (string trimmers). This cost the least of them all. I took out of the box and was delighted on how well it was built. The connecting rod is grooved. The spindle is grooved (gear type). The clamps are cast aluminum. All the pieces are equal or better than I expected. The 52cc with the blade attachment goes through just about anything. I beat the living heck out of it for 2 1/2 hours assuming it would fail. It surprised me. Not one stall, no problems yet. Cons: it weighs a bit more than a 64 year old guy want to carry around. The harness is lacking in its design. The instructions are so minimal your not sure about how to get the thing together (but not hard to figure out). All and all, pleasantly surprised. f",
